<p>Two vendors are in the middle of ownership changes. Roche announced in May 2026 an agreement to acquire PathAI, and Tempus announced a deal to acquire Paige in 2025. We have not confirmed that either has closed, so check who you would be contracting with.</p>

<h2 id="how-to-choose">How to choose in six questions</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Is it cleared for your region and your exact use?</strong> A cleared viewer is not a cleared AI algorithm. Ask for the clearance of each module you plan to use, for your tissue type, stain and scanner.</li>
<li><strong>Does it work with your scanner and slides?</strong> Many clearances name specific scanners and exclude frozen sections, cytology or special stains.</li>
<li><strong>Has it been validated on your own cases?</strong> Stain, scanning and population differences change performance. Run a local validation before reporting from it.</li>
<li><strong>Does it fit your LIS and workflow?</strong> Results should reach the pathologist inside the normal worklist, not on a separate screen.</li>
<li><strong>Where do slides and data go?</strong> Ask about cloud hosting, storage costs, de-identification and your local privacy rules.</li>
<li><strong>Who is responsible?</strong> The AI assists. The pathologist signs out the case and stays accountable for it.</li>
</ol>

<div class="callout"><b>Note:</b> a regulatory clearance shows a tool met a safety and effectiveness standard for a stated use. It does not show the tool will improve your diagnoses or save your laboratory time. Vendor claims here are the vendor’s own, not our findings.</div>

